<html lang="en"><head><title>Ridge trail 7</title><meta name="corten-scripts" content="/assets/scripts/"><meta name="corten-shell" content="c21cf50c33ce3fc2"><script type="importmap">{"imports":{"corten":"/corten/e3a8e75c9bf3/corten.js"}}</script><script type="module" src="/corten/e3a8e75c9bf3/corten.js"></script></head><body><header><p>Shared catalog of walking routes</p></header><main><h1>Ridge trail 7</h1><p>Archive entry 7, recorded 2026-10-03, last walked 2026-11-14.</p><p>A circular walking route through the landscape north of Greystone, recorded for the shared catalog. It climbs from the north gate through the beech wood to the ridge, follows the ridge west to the trig point and returns by the plantation, the village and the river. Read the notes and related records before setting out.</p><dl><div><dt>Access</dt><dd>Access notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Area</dt><dd>Area notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Archive</dt><dd>Archive notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd>Boundary notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Condition notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Direction</dt><dd>Direction notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Environment</dt><dd>Environment notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Feature</dt><dd>Feature notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Ground</dt><dd>Ground notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Habitat</dt><dd>Habitat notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Information</dt><dd>Information notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Journey</dt><dd>Journey notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Key</dt><dd>Key notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Location notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Material</dt><dd>Material notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Notes</dt><dd>Notes notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Origin</dt><dd>Origin notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Path</dt><dd>Path notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Quality</dt><dd>Quality notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Route</dt><dd>Route notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Surface</dt><dd>Surface notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Terrain</dt><dd>Terrain notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>Use</dt><dd>Use notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div><div><dt>View</dt><dd>View notes for entry 7: North gate, woodland path and open ground.</dd></div></dl><h2>Stages</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Distance</th><th>Surface</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>North gate to the old mill</td><td>1.2 km</td><td>Gravel</td><td>Level; the mill race is fenced on the left.</td></tr><tr><td>Old mill to Larch bridge</td><td>0.8 km</td><td>Packed earth</td><td>Wet after rain; boards over the two soft stretches.</td></tr><tr><td>Larch bridge to the beech wood</td><td>1.5 km</td><td>Earth and roots</td><td>Steady climb of 60 m; benches at the bend.</td></tr><tr><td>Through the beech wood</td><td>2.1 km</td><td>Leaf litter</td><td>Waymarked every 200 m; keep to the upper path.</td></tr><tr><td>Beech wood to Hollins farm</td><td>0.9 km</td><td>Farm track</td><td>Gates to close behind you; cattle from May.</td></tr><tr><td>Hollins farm to the ridge stile</td><td>1.1 km</td><td>Grass</td><td>Steepest part of the route, 110 m of ascent.</td></tr><tr><td>Along the ridge, west</td><td>2.6 km</td><td>Short turf</td><td>Open ground with views north; exposed in wind.</td></tr><tr><td>Ridge cairn to the trig point</td><td>0.7 km</td><td>Stony</td><td>Loose stones near the top; the pillar is 412 m.</td></tr><tr><td>Trig point to Saddle pool</td><td>1.4 km</td><td>Peat</td><td>Boggy in winter; flagstones laid across the worst.</td></tr><tr><td>Saddle pool to the larch plantation</td><td>1.0 km</td><td>Forest road</td><td>Timber lorries on weekdays; walk facing traffic.</td></tr><tr><td>Through the plantation</td><td>1.8 km</td><td>Forest road</td><td>Shade all day; the road forks twice, keep right.</td></tr><tr><td>Plantation edge to Greystone</td><td>1.3 km</td><td>Lane</td><td>Quiet lane between walls; passing places only.</td></tr><tr><td>Greystone to the chapel</td><td>0.6 km</td><td>Pavement</td><td>Through the village; shop and water tap by the green.</td></tr><tr><td>Chapel to the river path</td><td>0.9 km</td><td>Gravel</td><td>Steps down to the river; a ramp avoids them.</td></tr><tr><td>River path, downstream</td><td>2.4 km</td><td>Earth</td><td>Floods at the meadow in spate; a high path is signed.</td></tr><tr><td>Weir to the stepping stones</td><td>0.5 km</td><td>Earth</td><td>The stones are impassable in high water; use the footbridge.</td></tr><tr><td>Stepping stones to Lower wood</td><td>1.0 km</td><td>Grass</td><td>Gentle rise across two fields; dogs on leads.</td></tr><tr><td>Lower wood to the quarry</td><td>1.2 km</td><td>Old track</td><td>The quarry edge is fenced; keep to the track.</td></tr><tr><td>Quarry to the reservoir dam</td><td>1.6 km</td><td>Tarmac path</td><td>Shared with cyclists; the dam is crossed on its crest.</td></tr><tr><td>Reservoir dam to the north gate</td><td>1.9 km</td><td>Gravel</td><td>Returns along the east shore to the start.</td></tr></tbody></table></main></body></html>